{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold, I, etc.</b> Meaning: this angel is the angel who redeems the fathers — not one of the ministering angels of the heavenly host, but a great angel, as is known to those who understand. For we acknowledge no intermediary angel other than He, blessed be He, and the Shekhinah of His might, which is unified with Him in the sod of (Zechariah 14:9) ״ה׳ אֶחָד וּשְׁמוֹ אֶחָד״ — HaShem is one and His name is one."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Translated ה׳ within the verse quotation as HaShem per divine-name rules, expanding the idiomatic address the verse requires."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:32:56.250849879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}